📊 Dashboard Features

1. Monthly Sales Trends

A line chart showing monthly sales performance and helping identify increases, decreases, and peak sales periods.

2. Top 10 Products by Sales

A horizontal bar chart highlighting the products generating the highest sales.

3. Sales by Category

A donut chart showing the contribution of different product categories to total sales.

4. Sales by Region

A bar chart comparing sales performance across different regions.

5. Sales by Payment Mode

A donut chart showing the distribution of sales across UPI, Credit Card, Cash, and Debit Card.

6. Interactive Slicers

The dashboard includes:

📅 Order Date

🌍 Region

🏷️ Category

📦 Product

🛠️ Tools & Technologies

Microsoft Power BI

Power Query – Data cleaning and transformation

DAX – KPI and analytical measures

Excel / CSV – Data source

Data Visualization – Interactive charts and dashboard design

🧹 Data Preparation

The dataset was prepared using Power Query:

Removed duplicate rows

Removed unnecessary columns

Handled blank/null values

Converted Order Date to Date format

Converted Quantity to Whole Number

Converted Sales and Profit to numeric/currency formats

Renamed columns where required

Verified data types and data quality

🧮 DAX Measures

Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Sales])

Total Profit = SUM(Sales[Profit])

Total Quantity = SUM(Sales[Quantity])

Total Orders = DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Order_ID])

Average Order Value = DIVIDE([Total Sales], [Total Orders])

Replace table/column names with the actual names in your Power BI model if they differ.

